From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:33:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] configure: use the host python and meson instead of a venv

qemu 11.1.2 port of
meta-xt-qemu/recipes-qemu/qemu/qemu/0114-configure-use-the-host-python-and-meson-not-a-venv.patch;
that patch's description has the reasoning and the measurements.

Ported: Same drop of the venv. The host python that configure found with
`command -v` stays $python (0114 set python=python3; the found one is
the interpreter the recipe passes with --python), and the `if test "$?"`
check that followed the venv line goes with it: after a plain
assignment it was always false, and its message spoke of a venv that is
no longer made. qemu 11.1.2 computes the venv meson in a new block
(get_pwd, EXESUF, Haiku); the port replaces that block's one meson line
with the host meson, as 0114 did, so its `cd pyvenv/bin` no longer fails
in the configure log. The comments name this patch, q11-013, and the
0114 it ports.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe specific; see the oe-core originals]
---
 configure | 12 +++++-------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 6ddfe4b53..26e636427 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -937,14 +937,11 @@ python="$(command -v "$python")"
 echo "python determined to be '$python'"
 echo "python version: $($python --version)"
 
-python="$($python -B "${source_path}/python/scripts/mkvenv.py" create pyvenv)"
-if test "$?" -ne 0 ; then
-    error_exit "python venv creation failed"
-fi
-
+# Yocto (q11-013, the port of 0114): no venv. $python stays the host interpreter
+# found above, and mkvenv is a no-op (the host meson is taken below).
 # Suppress writing compiled files
 python="$python -B"
-mkvenv="$python ${source_path}/python/scripts/mkvenv.py"
+mkvenv=true
 
 # Finish preparing the virtual environment using vendored .whl files.
 # Even if PyPI is allowed, we disallow it here to force installation
@@ -967,7 +964,8 @@ get_pwd() {
     fi
 }
 
-meson="$(cd pyvenv/bin; get_pwd)/meson"
+# Yocto (q11-013, the port of 0114): the host meson from PATH, not the venv one.
+meson=$(command -v meson)
 if [ -f "$meson$EXESUF" ]; then
   meson="$meson$EXESUF"
 fi
